<title>PERU: SOCCER-PERU BEAT BOLIVIA 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PERU BEAT BOLIVIA 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru beat Bolivia 2-1 (halftime</p>
<p>1-0) in a South American World Cup qualifier Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Peru - German Carthy (10), Jose Soto (51)</p>
<p>Bolivia - Luis Cristaldo (54)</p>
<p>Attendance: 43,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>		  P  W  D  L  F  A Pts</p>
<p> Paraguay    11  7  2  2  16  8 23</p>
<p> Argentina   12  6  4  2  18 11 22</p>
<p> Colombia    12  5  3  4  17 14 18</p>
<p> Chile	 11  4  4  3  22 14 16</p>
<p> Peru	  12  4  4  4  13 15 16</p>
<p> Ecuador     12  4  3  5  16 14 15</p>
<p> Bolivia     11  3  5  3  16 12 14</p>
<p> Uruguay     11  4  2  5  11 15 14</p>
<p> Venezuela   12  0  3  9   8 34  3</p>
<p>Next matches: July 20 - Argentina v Venezuela, Bolivia v</p>
<p>Uruguay, Colombia v Ecuador, Chile v Paraguay</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
